.TH SENDMSG 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
sendmsg \- send a scatter/gather socket message
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.B ssize_t sendmsg(int descriptor, const struct msghdr* message, int flags);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends data described by message and its iovec array.
Optional destination and control buffers use Linux kernel layouts.
The MSG_NOSIGNAL flag suppresses SIGPIPE for this call.
Crunch structures use the Linux x86\-64 ABI and are not portable layouts.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns bytes sent, possibly fewer than requested, or \-1 with errno set.
Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR recvmsg (3crunch),
.BR sendmsg (2)
